<Song resolves-to="SongSP" spName="MinorSwing-Dm-Theme" spTempo="144">
  <spVERSION>4</spVERSION>
  <spComments>Year:	1937
Composer:	Django Reinhardt and Stéphane Grappelli
Lyricist:	None — instrumental
Form:	16-bar repeating chord progression,
	with a short composed head and 
                          improvised solos
Style:	Gypsy jazz swing
Key:	A minor

“Minor Swing” was first recorded in 1937 by the Quintette
du Hot Club de France. Its compact, repeating minor-key
progression and opportunities for improvisation helped
make it a signature tune of the gypsy-jazz tradition.</spComments>
